            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Danielle Tremblay Duprey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it! I would like to reduce the amount of butter on top, does anyone has a suggestion?",
            "datePublished": "2013-10-02T02:18:43.777Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dee Stillwell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This pumpkin cake was very good, altho I think I like my recipe that uses a 29 oz can pf pumpkin better, as it has a better pie filling to topping ratio &amp; makes it more pumpkin pie-ish. I like the use of brown sugar and more spice than the norm. I always dbl the spice in my pumpkin pie. Since I only had a 15 1/2 oz can of pumpkin, this is the recipe I used. I didn't have pecans or walnuts so used sliced almonds instead and added flaked coconut for some crunch. I cut the melted butter back to 3/4 cup. It was served with fresh whipped cream and it tasted delicious.",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-27T21:12:45.733Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessie's Mom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is our Favorite Cake - I have used a receipe similar to this for several years with a few minor differences - only use 2 tsp. Pumpkin Pie Spice, granulated sugar, 4 eggs plus 1 tsp. salt",
            "datePublished": "2009-11-15T13:13:23.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Suzanne"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Way too sweet. I reduced the sugar to 1/4 c. There is enough sugar in the cake mix and milk that a full cup is not needed. I like to taste the flavors of ingredients, not the sugar.",
            "datePublished": "2009-06-04T19:34:33.517Z"
          }
